  "question": {
    "text": "Two poles standing on a horizontal ground are of heights <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>m</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>m</mi></math> respectively. The line joining their tops makes an angle of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> with the ground. Then the distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo></math>in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;between the poles, is",
    "image": null
  },
